# Fuzzing runtime artifacts — all regenerated, never committed.

# Seed corpus: cmd/seedgen rebuilds it on every run.
fuzz/corpus/

# Crash + report output written by scripts/fuzz.sh ($FINDINGS), one dir per run.
# Ignore the crashers, reproducers and per-target logs, but KEEP each run's
# SUMMARY.md report (the table + reach/impact verdict) under version control.
# The directory contents are ignored (not the directory itself) so the SUMMARY
# negation can re-include — git cannot re-include a file under a fully-ignored
# directory.
fuzz/findings/*
fuzz/findings-*/*

# Captured run logs (per-target *.fuzz.log, panic dumps) and sweep/coverage output.
*.log
*.out

# Build / test binaries.
*.exe
*.test

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/

# NOTE: fuzz/**/testdata/fuzz/ is deliberately NOT ignored — those are the
# committed regression reproducers, the point of the whole tree. go-zenon/ is a
# git submodule pinned to the fuzzed commit (see .gitmodules), not ignored.
